WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.250
In the eighth century BC,
the kings of Urartu

2
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.819
ruled the highlands around Lake Van
from their rock citadel at Tushpa.

3
00:00:10.859 --> 00:00:13.059
They called their land Biainili.

4
00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:16.629
Under Argishti I, son of Menua,

5
00:00:16.669 --> 00:00:19.305
the kingdom stood
near the height of its power.

6
00:00:19.345 --> 00:00:21.793
He pushed north of the Araxes.

7
00:00:22.153 --> 00:00:26.183
There, in 782 BC,
he raised a new fortress

8
00:00:26.223 --> 00:00:28.083
on the hill of Arin Berd,

9
00:00:28.123 --> 00:00:30.492
and named it Erebuni.

10
00:00:30.852 --> 00:00:34.282
His founding inscription,
cut in cuneiform,

11
00:00:34.322 --> 00:00:36.966
was found on the hill in 1950.

12
00:00:37.326 --> 00:00:39.756
Argishti also fought Assyria,

13
00:00:39.796 --> 00:00:43.100
but those wars were fought
far from Erebuni.

14
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.819
From its walls, Urartu's kings
struck north toward Lake Sevan.

15
00:00:48.179 --> 00:00:50.869
Yet the name lives on in Yerevan,

16
00:00:50.909 --> 00:00:53.931
which counts its birth
from Argishti's stone.

17
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:57.814
Defend the young city.

